A key-less variant's title is its own name in a union without a catch-all: a
discriminator equal to it decodes into the variant, strictly, as a named
variant's value does. A type no variant names is still kept in Unknown
(0011-MADR-harden-code-generator-engine.md, F1). In a union with a catch-all
the title is a label, not a wire value, and the catch-all keeps taking it
(0049-PLAN-surface-fixes.md, phase 1, deviations 1 and 2).
The meta declares $/cancel_request and the schema its smallest definition, which
the runtime needs.

-- meta.json --
{"version": 1, "agentMethods": {}, "clientMethods": {}, "protocolMethods": {"cancel_request": "$/cancel_request"}}
-- schema.json --
{"$defs": {
  "U": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "a"}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"title": "loose", "type": "object", "required": ["x"], "properties": {"x": {"type": "string"}}}]},
  "C": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "a"}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"title": "other", "type": "object", "required": ["type"], "properties": {"type": {"type": "string"}}, "not": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "a"}}, "required": ["type"]}]}}, {"title": "plain", "type": "object", "required": ["y"], "properties": {"y": {"type": "string"}}}]},
  "CancelRequestNotification": {"type": "object", "x-side": "protocol", "x-method": "$/cancel_request"}
}}
-- want.api --
